WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.050
A coastline receives sediment from local erosion and from rivers, waves

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.410
and currents. A beach can contain sand, shells or rounded gravel;

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.410
not every coast has a sandy beach.

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:14.950
Long narrow accumulations of sand can form barrier islands.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:19.810
Shallow lagoons or saltwater marshes commonly separate those islands from the

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:20.130
mainland.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:24.690
A lagoon is sheltered water behind a reef or island.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.810
Its nearshore sediment may come from land, while coral and shell

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:30.290
debris can enter from a reef.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:34.990
In suitable shallow, warm, clear water, organisms build reefs from their

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:39.110
hard parts. The reef reduces the wave energy reaching the protected

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:39.710
shoreline.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:44.610
Continental shelves and slopes accumulate mud, sand and carbonate material.

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:48.870
When sediment becomes unstable, a dense mixture of water and sediment

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.650
can move downslope as a turbidity current.

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:55.190
Submarine canyons may funnel this material toward deeper water.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:59.570
Quiet offshore settling and sudden downslope transport can occur in the

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.190
same basin.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:03.050
Deep seafloor is cold and dark.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:07.850
Far from land, fine windblown dust and microscopic marine remains commonly

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:12.270
dominate the sediment. Along a shoreline, tidal flats alternate between flooding

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.470
and exposure. In hot dry settings, evaporation can leave salt and

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:19.410
other minerals. Depth alone does not explain every deposit.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:23.850
Wind can carry beach sand inland to coastal dunes and can

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.570
return it toward the water when wind direction changes.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:31.750
Deltas extend offshore, where unstable fronts can deliver sediment to deeper

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.990
water. Read the whole system:

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:39.850
sediment supply, water clarity, organisms, wave protection and transport all help

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.630
distinguish neighboring environments.
